    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25im6tek3hPTzw72mkyzRzY)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on current `main` (after #518, #519, #520); independent of the other open PRs.\n- Touches the lint part of `sp-academic.org` / `sp-bibprocess.el` (`sp-bibtex-lint--save`, the `sp-bibtex-merge--*` functions), so it may conflict with other open lint PRs.\n\n## What I found\n\n- The command is `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-merge` (the only merge lint; also step 4 of `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors`).\n- It already reverted the visiting buffer through `sp-bibtex-lint--save`, shared by every write-capable lint fix (date, duplicates, authors, organisations, files, keys, crossref).\n- Gaps in that shared helper:\n  - a buffer with unsaved changes was skipped silently, so it stayed stale;\n  - citar's cache was refreshed only by the long-keys fix;\n  - the merge checks for unsaved changes only when it starts, but its questions can take a while.\n- The abstract mover has its own `sp-bibtex-abstract--refresh-buffer` (revert plus vulpea update); left alone to keep the diff small.\n- The merge had no way to drop groups; the other fixes drop entries with `d` and restore with `u`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Reload (shared by all lint writers):\n  - New `sp-bibtex-lint--refresh`, called by `sp-bibtex-lint--save`: reverts the unmodified buffer without a question (point stays), never discards unsaved edits (warns instead), refreshes citar.\n  - New `sp-bibtex-lint--unsaved-resolve`, used by `sp-bibtex-merge--apply` just before writing: with unsaved changes asks `d` diff, `r` recheck after saving, `s` skip (nothing written).\n- Drop and restore (merge only):\n  - In the group question: `d` drops the group for later, `u` brings a dropped group back.\n  - Dropped groups are skipped going forward, also in later runs of the Emacs session; `p` can step back to one to restore it.\n  - Stored in `sp-bibtex-lint--excluded` with key `FILE::TARGET#merge`, so `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-restore-dropped` lists and restores them with the dropped entries.\n  - When every group is dropped, the command says so and asks nothing.\n- Docs updated as bullets in `sp-academic.org`, re-tangled to `sp-bibprocess.el`.\n- `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## What is not verified\n\n- Tested only with standalone Emacs 29.3 batch scripts on the new functions (reload and warn on unsaved; skip choice; `d` dropping a group and skipping it). The existing lint test file could not be loaded in the container (dependency chain), so the full suite was not run.\n- The report view (dashboard section and `sp-bibtex-merge--text`) still lists dropped groups; only the question skips them.\n- The batch report view is not refreshed after a write (no other fix does it either).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Open a `.bib` file in a buffer (no edits). `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-merge`, merge a group, `yes`: the buffer shows the new names with no prompt and point stays near where it was\n- [ ] Start the merge, and before the final `yes` type a character in the `.bib` buffer: at the write you get the `d`/`r`/`s` question\n- [ ] `d` shows a diff of your unsaved change; `s` writes nothing and the buffer keeps the change; saving the buffer and pressing `r` goes on and rewrites\n- [ ] After a merge, citar completion shows the new author names without restarting\n- [ ] In the group question, `d` on a group: the next group is asked; run the command again: the dropped group is not asked\n- [ ] `p` back to the dropped group shows \"(dropped for later)\"; `u` restores it and it is asked again next time\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-restore-dropped` lists the dropped group (as `NAME#merge`) and brings it back\n- [ ] Drop every group: the command says the groups left are dropped and asks nothing\n- [ ] Regression: `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-date` and `-fix-duplicates` still revert an unmodified buffer after `A`\n- [ ] Regression: `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors` still runs all steps and ends with the merge\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBu9gSrA6zCRACfDk4)_\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBu9gSrA6zCRACfDk4)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBu9gSrA6zCRACfDk4",
